From af4595872279fc9889e3cc9957727a803d5741cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:08:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: mempool admission, rejections, fee rates, removals
 and orphans

The mempool's size was exported, but not the flow through it: how many
transactions are accepted or refused and why, at what fee rates, how they
leave, what the admission floor is, and how many orphans wait outside.

- fullnode_mempool_accepted_total, and
  fullnode_mempool_rejected_total{reason}: one reason per
  TxValidationResult (13: consensus, inputs_not_standard, not_standard,
  missing_inputs, premature_spend, duplicate, conflict,
  child_before_parent, mempool_policy, no_mempool,
  package_reconsiderable, avalanche_reconsiderable, unknown), a fixed list
  rather than the open-ended reject strings. A package member already in
  the mempool counts as duplicate. Recorded where single transactions
  (AcceptToMemoryPool), packages (ProcessNewPackage) and raw batches
  (ProcessRawTxBatch) get their final result; test acceptances are not
  counted. Acceptances include reorg re-additions and the mempool file.
- fullnode_mempool_accepted_fee_rate_sats_per_byte (histogram): each
  accepted transaction's base fee over its virtual size, recorded in
  sat/kB, 18 bounds from 0 to 10000 sat/byte, dense around the default
  1 sat/byte floor.
- fullnode_mempool_removed_total{reason}: the seven MemPoolRemovalReasons
  (expiry and sizelimit are the evictions), counted in removeUnchecked;
  label values match RemovalReasonToString (unit-tested).
- fullnode_mempool_min_fee_rate_sats_per_byte{kind=rolling|effective}:
  the rolling minimum (getmempoolinfo's mempoolminfee before the relay
  floor) and the effective admission floor (estimatefee), set at scrape
  time; this takes mempool.cs briefly, as those RPCs do.
- fullnode_tx_pool_transactions{pool=orphan|conflicting} (scrape time,
  each pool's own mutex) and fullnode_tx_pool_removed_total{pool,
  reason=expired|evicted}, counted in TxPool::LimitTxs.

Cardinality: accepted 1, rejected 13, fee rate histogram 1 (19
buckets), removed 7, min fee rate 2, tx pool 2, tx pool removed 4.

Hot paths: one sharded counter add per admission result (plus one ring
push for an acceptance), one per mempool removal, one per LimitTxs call
that removed something. All under locks already held (cs_main,
mempool.cs, the pool mutex); no lock is added. Benches at the end of the
series.

Evidence:
- metrics_tests (new: reject reason per TxValidationResult, removal
  labels equal RemovalReasonToString), mempool_tests, orphanage_tests,
  txpool_tests, txvalidation_tests pass.
- interface_metrics_mempool.py: an accepted transaction counts once and
  its fee rate (fee over size) lands in the right bucket; a
  missing-input and an overspending transaction count as missing_inputs
  and consensus, testmempoolaccept is not counted; a mined transaction
  counts as removed for block, an expired one (mock time past
  -mempoolexpiry) as expiry; the rolling floor is 0 and the effective one
  matches estimatefee and is at least minrelaytxfee; with
  -maxorphantx=1, two orphans from a P2P peer leave one held and one
  evicted.

Not tested: package and raw batch admission results (same recording
function), sizelimit evictions, orphan expiry, a full mempool's rolling
fee.
